
---

## 3) `.gitignore`

For your **Python_Programming GitHub repository**, use this professional Python-specific `.gitignore`:

```gitignore
# ==============================================================
# Python_Programming - Git Ignore
# ==============================================================

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# Python cache
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# Distribution / packaging
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/
.eggs/

# Jupyter Notebook
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Coverage reports
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/

# Test reports
.pytest_cache/

# IDE settings
.vscode/
.idea/

# Operating system files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Environment / secret files
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Logs
*.log

# Temporary files
*.tmp
*.temp

# Python profiling
*.prof

# Local databases
*.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3

# Model / large generated files
*.pkl
*.pickle
*.joblib

# ==============================================================
# End
# ==============================================================